The mimic adaptation removes participant identifiers, resamples the sensor
streams, aggregates gestures by context/hand/direction, and stores only group
means and low-rank principal components. It does not contain source records or
individual gesture traces.

The built-in regional catalog is derived from Unicode CLDR 48.0.0 and
IANA tzdb 2026c zone.tab. It selects documented official languages (or the
most widely used recorded language where none is official), filters for
available CLDR language/script data, and pairs national languages with
country time zones. Regional-only languages are omitted for multi-zone
territories. These are derived configurations, not observed user profiles.
Source URLs and SHA-256 digests are included in the compiled catalog.
